.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt UUDECODE 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm uudecode
.Nd decode a POSIX uuencode stream
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Ar input
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads a POSIX
.Ql begin Ns / Ns Ql end
stream from
.Ar input
(or standard input when omitted), validates the encoded lines and writes the
decoded bytes to the name in the header, or to
.Ar output
when
.Fl o
is supplied.
The stored mode is applied to the output file.
.Pp
Path-like encoded names are rejected when no explicit
.Fl o
path is given.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Invalid input, an unsafe encoded name or an I/O error exits nonzero.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ar 1 ,
.Xr uuencode 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the POSIX uudecode format.
